Id: con014e
Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: config
Fix: Give --root the mounted image's top directory, the one with etc in it.
References: tigris(8)

The directory given with --root is not the root of a system Tigris can
audit: it does not exist, has no etc directory, or its path has
characters other than letters, digits and / . _ + @ : , = - (a space, a
quote), which the checks would split or misread. --root audits a
system that is not running, a disk image mounted somewhere, a container
image unpacked, a backup, from outside it: the checks read its files
under that directory, follow its symbolic links inside it, and ask the
host's own package tools about its databases (dpkg --admindir, rpm
--root). Nothing from the audited system is run. The run stops before
any check, so that a mistyped path does not quietly audit the host
itself. Checks that read the running system (processes, listening
ports, the firewall, the kernel's settings) are skipped and listed in
the report as such.
